course: dictionary
lesson: 4423
title: Words from other lands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hammock is a bed made of cloth or net, hung between two trees or posts, that you lie in and can swing. Long ago, sailors on ships slept in hammocks hung between beams.
explain: Context helps you understand it. «Words such as hammock, canoe and hurricane came into English from the Taíno language.» The sentence tells you that hammock is one of a group of words borrowed from another language.
explain: A comparison can build a picture in your head. «Two twisty white cords hold the yolk in the middle like the ropes of a hammock.» Ropes hold a hammock up at each end, so the cords hold the yolk up in the middle, just as a hammock is held up.
fact: A hammock is a bed made of cloth or net that hangs between two trees or posts.
fact: Sailors on old ships slept in hammocks hung between beams.
fact: The word hammock came into English from the Taíno people of the Caribbean.
fact: Canoe and hurricane also came into English from the Taíno language.
fact: «Hammock» is a noun: one hammock, two hammocks.
exercise: Which picture matches a hammock? | A metal chair with four legs | A boat with oars and a sail | * A bed made of cloth or net, hung between two trees, that you can swing in | A small wooden box for toys
exercise: «Words such as hammock, canoe and hurricane came into English from the Taíno language.» Where did hammock come from? | The school library | French food words | * The Taíno language | The seaside pier
exercise: «Two twisty white cords hold the yolk in the middle like the ropes of a hammock.» What does the comparison show you? | The cords are made of wool | * The cords hold the yolk up at each end, like a hammock | The yolk is swinging from a tree | The yolk is cold and wet
test: «The sailors slept in hammocks hung between the beams of the ship.» Where were the hammocks hung? | Inside a wooden box | Between two trees | On the beach under the sun | * Between beams on a ship
test: Which word in «Words such as hammock, canoe and hurricane came into English» is a word from the Taíno language? | English | * Hurricane | Came | Words
exam: «In the garden, Ella lay in her hammock and swung gently under the apple tree.» Why is the hammock a clue to a relaxed, sunny moment? | Hammocks are always made of metal | Hammocks are used for cooking food | Hammocks are used for lazing and swinging, so she is calm and at ease | * Hammocks are only used for sleeping in the dark
